{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The original house has a footprint of less than 130 square metres and is therefore unsuitable for conversion to flats. As such the application is unacceptable in principle and fails to comply with Local Plan policy SC6.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposal would be excessively bulky and domineering. The proposal would fail to relate subordinately to the main property and would have a convoluted and contrived appearance that would result in harm to the character and appearance of the local area. The proposal would be unacceptable in terms of its design contrary to Local Plan policies CC1 and CC2 as well as the council's design guidance.",
    "Reason : 3 - The application has failed to demonstrate that the proposal would be exempt from BNG and without evidence to the contrary the proposal would fail to achieve an acceptable Biodiversity Net Gain contrary to London Plan policies G6 and G7 and Local Plan policy BG7.",
    "Reason : 4 - Due to the excessive projection and proximity to the neighbouring properties the proposal would result in a loss of outlook and light as well as a sense of enclosure to neighbouring occupiers contrary to Local Plan policies CC1 and CC2 as well as the council's design guidance.",
    "Reason : 5 - Due to the insufficient Gross Internal Area (GIA) of the first floor flat and in the absence of evidence to show that this unit would benefit from a sufficient and readily accessible provision of outdoor amenity space, the proposal has failed to demonstrate an acceptable quality of accommodation for future occupiers, contrary to The Nationally Described Space Standards, London Plan policy D6 and Local Plan policy SC5.",
    "Reason : 6 - Without evidence to the contrary the proposal would fail to provide adequate storage space for waste and recycling bins within the site frontage contrary to London Plan policy D6 and Local Plan policy EQ7.",
    "Reason : 7 - Without evidence to the contrary the proposal would result in harm to the safety and efficiency of the local transport network and would fail to provide an acceptable level of secure cycle parking for future occupiers contrary to London Plan policies T4 and T5 as well as Local Plan policy EC2."
  ],
